speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I appreciate the question of the Deputy House Leader of the Official Opposition. In responding to the Hon. Member's question, I should like to advise the House that there have been discussions between the Parties. I
February 14, 1985

believe, Mr. Speaker, that if you were to seek unanimous consent of the House to put the following motion, that consent would be forthcoming. The order is as follows:
That the Standing Committee on Miscellaneous Estimates be empowered to examine and report on the advisibility of
(a)	Canada issuing a circulating dollar coin;
(b)	the raising of funds for the 1988 Calgary Olympics through assigning the seigniorage from the first issue of such coins to the Calgary Olympics; and
(c)	the size, shape, and composition of any such dollar coin if it were to be issued;
That the Committee have the power to retain the services of expert, professional, technical and clerical staff as may be deemed necessary;
That the Committee submit an estimate of expenses to be incurred in the exercise of its authority to hire to the House of Commons for concurrence prior to proceeding with its inquiry; and
That the Committee report back to the House not later than June 14, 1985.
